

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 1

                                  FOR

                 SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU




         




  Quote of the Week:

  Saint Ignatius Loyola, Spanish soldier and founder of the Jesuit Order, 
1522:
  "To arrive at the truth in all things, we ought always to be ready to 
believe that what seems to us white, is black if the hierarchical Church so 
defines it."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Uga-Buga Makumb tried hard to improve his Necromancy, but he 
practiced in vain.
  With the advent of the early summer season, Uga-Buga Makumb practiced his 
Necromancy and his skill in Necromancy went up.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a pleasant late summer arrived.  
Uga-Buga Makumb worked on his Necromancy but was thwarted in his efforts.
  In fall, Teleko levied the 240th Bowmen and the 241st Bowmen in the 
Dolphin Sea to serve Uga-Buga Makumb.  Teleko hired the 209th Warg Riders, a 
mercenary army which had arrived in the Dolphin Sea.
  Uga-Buga Makumb marched on the Virgo Sea (#1005) with his formidable 
forces.  Viewing the northeastern horizon, a man can see a Forest province 
known as Kildare (#1004).  It is said that Magnus is the ruler there.  It is 
known to be occupied by Elves.  Their Elven warriors array themselves as 
Legion and Chariots.  To the west there is a Sea province known as the 
Amazonian Sea (#905), a prosperous area of no races where no one rules.  
Northwest of here is the Sixth Sea (#904), a prosperous Sea province ruled 
by no one, where Whales dwell.  If need be, they can muster an army of 
Whales to defend their province.

  Soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Uga-Buga Makumbian empire 
marched on the Forest province of the Virgo Sea, a land defended by the 
soldiers of Melantheus (#30).  Uga-Buga Makumb commanded the attacking 
armies.  The defenders were led by Melantheus.  The armies were drawn up 
into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Virgo Sea (1005):

