  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with his warriors was 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Lord of the stu.  Melantheus marched with his loyal 
troops, eyes set in terrible resolution.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The contest was a fair fight, as no luck or mischance of 
great significance appeared to affect the overall engagement before it 
started.  As the struggle intensified, the tactical abilities of Melantheus 
and Uga-Buga Makumb appeared well matched.

  Out on the left outside wing, the 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
107th Heavy Cavalry, who shouted their war cries, whipped into a terrible  
fanatical frenzy by their diabolical King with promises of easy plunder.  
The 241st Bowmen outflanked the enemy and charged in with full strength.  On 
this battleground, the men of the 107th Heavy Cavalry had lost sleep because 
of the bad local food and became slightly ill.  They went into battle at a 
minor disadvantage.  The 110th Bowmen battled with the 107th Heavy Cavalry 
and ground ahead slowly, battled for every yard of their advance.
  Out on the right wing, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed against the 
106th Axemen.  The 240th Bowmen flanked the undermanned enemy and attacked 
with full strength.  In this sector, the 106th Axemen were at first slow to 
join battle, but when a brave little squire picked up a dagger and said 
"I'll show you how to fight!"  , they were so inspired that they 
determinedly charged into battle.  In spite of the 106th Axemen's good luck, 
the 108th Skeletal Bowmen fought the 106th Axemen and gradually shoved them 
back.
  The host of Uga-Buga Makumb finally crushed the army of Melantheus's 
morale with one last, great push.  The 240th Bowmen gave chase and scattered 
the 106th Axemen in all directions.
  Uga-Buga Makumb's host concluded the campaign successfully and conquered 
the province of the Virgo Sea.  The 107th Heavy Cavalry were unable to 
escape and were disbanded into the population.
  The fall cooled into early winter.  Uga-Buga Makumb marched on the 
Jellyfish Sea (#1105) with his forces.  Northeast of here is Mare Ionium 
(#1104), a prosperous Sea area ruled by no one, where no races dwell.  
Looking to the east, one can see a poor Jungle area, which is known as 
Kumasi (#1205).  It is populated by Trolls and no one rules there.  If need 
be, they can muster a host of Trolls to defend their province.


  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Lord of the stu's forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at the Jellyfish Sea, a Forest province owing its 
allegiance to Tao-Li (#32).  Uga-Buga Makumb commanded the invading armies.  
The defenders were led by Tao-Li.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Jellyfish Sea (1105):

