  DEFENDING ARMY

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Lord of the stu led his armies into the fray.  
Tao-Li stood determinedly at the head of his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  His luck didn't hold up this time.  His superstitious men 
became unsettled when his priests were unable to properly sacrifice a bull 
to the Great Father because they had all been stolen by racketeers.  Also, 
his tactical plans failed to work out as expected against Tao-Li's prompt 
counterstrokes, and his forces fought with a small tactical disadvantage.

  On the left outside wing, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 121st Fleet 
Marines.  The 109th Heavy Cavalry flanked the undermanned enemy lines and 
charged in with full force.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 121st 
Fleet Marines and quickly knifed into them.
  Within the interior lines, the 240th Bowmen were arrayed against the 120th 
Axemen.  In this match, the spirits of the soldiers of the 240th Bowmen were 
raised when one sergeant yelled "Long live our glorious Commander!"  , and 
the rallying cry was echoed by all of the 240th Bowmen.  The 240th Bowmen 
fought with the 120th Axemen and could neither gain the advantage nor could 
the enemy make any progress.
  On the right outside flank, the 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
122nd Axemen.  Here, some gossip was circulated among the 110th Bowmen that 
they would receive medals if they performed well, which gave the 110th 
Bowmen the psychological edge.  The 110th Bowmen fought the 122nd Axemen and 
the fighting here was inconclusive.
  Having found a weak spot in the line of the host of Tao-Li, a final 
determined slashing attack defeated their enemy and won the battle for 
Uga-Buga Makumb.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen destroyed the 121st Fleet 
Marines.  The 109th Heavy Cavalry pursued the enemy and were beaten off by 
the 120th Axemen in a hard-fought rearguard battle.  The 209th Warg Riders 
gave chase and annihilated the 120th Axemen.
  The Jellyfish Sea was overrun by Uga-Buga Makumb's men in a hard-fought 
campaign.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen proved its valor during the battle and we now rank it a 
Veteran unit.  The 241st Bowmen was greatly inspired by the exciting battle. 
We now designate it a Veteran unit.  The 122nd Axemen were unable to escape 
and were paroled into the population.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Lord of the stu for 
this year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb asked Lord Babba Sissoko Master of the s (#0) to improve 
relations with his Kingdom, speaking at length of the great benefits of such 
an agreement.  After some deliberation, the offer was wisely accepted by 
Babba Sissoko.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Lord of the stu has been informed by Circe (#8) 
that his cooperation has become unnecessary, and thus our formerly amicable 
relations are now severed.
  Agesilao (#9) urged Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Lord of the stu to improve 
relations with his great Kingdom, speaking eloquently of the great benefits 
of such an agreement.  After some deliberation, the proposal was graciously 
accepted by Uga-Buga Makumb.


  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 26 gold in revenue.  4 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  14 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Uga-Buga Makumb was 
left with 11 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Montgomery, Squire to Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Guerin was tutored in Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  Guerin 
practiced enthusiastically and improved his ability in Necromancy.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Guerin was 
tutored in Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  Guerin practiced his Necromancy 
and improved noticeably.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Guerin was instructed in the 
art of Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  Guerin practiced his Necromancy and 
his skill in Necromancy went up.
  During fall, Guerin dropped off the 108th Skeletal Bowmen, the 109th 
Heavy Cavalry and the 110th Bowmen in the Dolphin Sea for Uga-Buga Makumb.
  The fall season darkened into the stillness of early winter.  Guerin cast 
a Plague spell.  The Mermaid Sea was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 
96th Bowmen in the Mermaid Sea and destroyed them.  His efforts raised his 
aptitude in Necromancy.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I was tutored in Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  I practiced 
hard for months and my skill in Necromancy increased.
  In early summer, I was tutored in Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  I 
practiced well and improved my ability in Necromancy.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  I was 
instructed in the art of Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  I rehearsed and 
practiced my Necromancy and improved noticeably.
  With the coming of the fall season, I levied the 240th Bowmen and the 
241st Bowmen in the Dolphin Sea to serve Uga-Buga Makumb.  I hired the 209th 
Warg Riders, a mercenary army which had arrived in the Dolphin Sea.
  The fall season darkened into the stillness of early winter.  I cast a 
Plague spell.  The Icaria Sea was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 
111th Legion in the Icaria Sea and destroyed them.

  Thy humble servant,   Teleko


